1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:28,440
A Real Stewart

2
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:29,900
It's almost ten o'clock.

3
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:33,420
I've got to go. Tomorrow is Monday,

4
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:35,900
and work begins at eight in the morning for me.

5
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:37,920
Oh, I'm so happy that Max is home.

6
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:40,550
He's the sweetest little thing.

7
00:00:40,550 --> 00:00:42,510
I'll drive you to the station, dear.

8
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:46,520
You can catch the ten-twenty train to Grand Central Station.

9
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:48,710
I'll drive Susan, dear.

10
00:00:48,710 --> 00:00:50,140
Thank you, Philip.

11
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:51,510
Then Grandpa, Robbie,

12
00:00:51,510 --> 00:01:12,230
and I can finish wrapping all these gifts.

13
00:01:12,230 --> 00:01:16,230
It's so good to have you home again ...

14
00:01:16,230 --> 00:01:22,780
and to see Max asleep in his bassinet at home with us.

15
00:01:22,780 --> 00:01:29,320
To be with our family and all that Stewart TLC.

16
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:36,270
TLC--tender loving care.

17
00:01:36,270 --> 00:01:39,890
That's our motto.

18
00:01:39,890 --> 00:01:40,990
Did you see the washcloth

19
00:01:40,990 --> 00:01:44,280
and the towels with the teddy bears on them?

20
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:47,840
Alexandra and the Molinas sent them for Max.

21
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:50,590
It was so kind of them.

22
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:52,880
Now Max has come into everyone's life.

23
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:56,510
The house is so alive with him here.

24
00:01:56,510 --> 00:01:59,970
The welcome sign over the door.

25
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:02,570
The boxes of presents.

26
00:02:02,570 --> 00:02:05,040
The M-A-X over his bassinet.

27
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:07,910
Robbie put that there.

28
00:02:07,910 --> 00:02:09,780
Susan's teddy bear.

29
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:17,450
So cuddly. The beautiful crib from Mom and Dad.

30
00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:22,090
Oh, and Grandpa's baseball glove.

31
00:02:22,090 --> 00:02:24,780
You know, it hung over my crib, too.

32
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:27,440
And it hung over Robbie's crib.

33
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:29,140
Part of Grandpa's magic?

34
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:31,010
Oh, that's not all.

35
00:02:31,010 --> 00:02:32,750
It hung over Susan's crib.

36
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:34,190
The same baseball glove?

37
00:02:34,190 --> 00:02:38,990
That's right. Grandpa hangs it there for good luck.

38
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:43,870
He says it always brought him good luck on the baseball team.

39
00:02:43,870 --> 00:02:47,980
He believes it'll bring good luck to all the Stewart babies.

40
00:02:47,980 --> 00:02:49,310
And then he takes it back

41
00:02:49,310 --> 00:02:50,090
when Max is ready to use it?

42
00:02:50,090 --> 00:02:51,130
Yes,

43
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:53,070
and replaces it with a new glove

44
00:02:53,070 --> 00:02:55,140
so the old one will be ready

45
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:58,730
for a new member of the Stewart family.

46
00:02:58,730 --> 00:03:04,280
Grandpa really loves his family, doesn't he?

47
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:07,050
So do I.

48
00:03:07,050 --> 00:03:14,590
And so do I.

49
00:03:14,590 --> 00:03:16,770
And so does Max.

50
00:03:16,770 --> 00:03:19,770
After he eats!
